  {
    "date": "2025-02-05",
    "term": "治める",
    "kana": "おさめる",
    "meaning": "to govern, to manage; to subdue",
    "level": "N3",
    "pos": ["Ichidan verb", "transitive verb"],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": [],
    "headline": "治める is from Old Japanese 治む (wosamu), and the source gives 収める (osameru) as a cognate.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese 治む (wosamu). Attested in the Nihon Shoki of 720 CE, and the Man'yōshū of circa 759 CE. Ultimately from Proto-Japonic *wosamu (“to control”). Cognate with 収(おさ)める (osameru)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Development"
      },
      {
        "quote": "Natural progression from Old and Classical Japanese 下(しも)二(に)段(だん)活(かつ)用(よう) (shimo nidan katsuyō, “lower bigrade conjugation”) verbs ending in -u to modern Japanese 下(しも)一(いち)段(だん)活(かつ)用(よう) (shimo ichidan katsuyō, “lower monograde conjugation”) verbs ending in -eru. For the Old / Classical form, see the 治む entry."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Likely derived ultimately from 長(おさ) (osa, “boss, chief, controller, ruler”)."
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
  },
